+# Research sources consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- **Broadcom VMware Hardware Compatibility Guide**
+  https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/
+  Consulted its interoperability and upgrade-path views to cross-check the
+  vCenter, ESX, and NSX target family for the 9.0.1-to-9.1 transition.
+
+- **Minimum number of ESXi hosts required on vSAN clusters for deployment of VCF Management Domain**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993/minimum-number-of-esxi-hosts-required-on.html
+  Confirmed that a single-availability-zone vSAN management domain has a
+  supported minimum of four ESXi hosts.
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  Informed the Operations-first sequence, the 12-address Management Services
+  pool on the management network, its 198.18.0.0/15 internal range, Fleet
+  Management retirement, Identity Broker migration, and downstream gates.
+
+- **Required Component Binaries for VCF 9.1 upgrade**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425089/required-component-binaries-for-vcf-91.html
+  Informed the binary-availability gate and the primary-instance management
+  service set.
+
+- **Could not retrieve binary for component during Deploy and Validate in VCF 9.1**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436258/could-not-retrieve-binary-for-component.html
+  Cross-checked that the installer JSON component builds must match the active
+  9.1 bill of materials rather than stale deployment values.
+
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs, tag 9.1.0.0 — VCF Installer OpenAPI**
+  https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json
+  Informed the exact SddcSpec field structure, required fields, network types,
+  vSAN FTT representation, and VCF Management Services address-pool shape.
